    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d800">

                <pb facs="0813" n="701" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg701"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860d.51/9: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Viborg</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Imbrie</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Viborg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-16"><hi rendition="#italic">August 16,
                        1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 17, 1:42 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>81. I am confidentially informed through Russian General Staff that the recent
                    loans of £6,000,000 made by the British to the Finnish Government had as a
                    condition that the Finns should mobilize and <pb facs="0814" n="702"
                        xml:id="pg702"/> start an offensive with Petrograd as the objective, the
                    capitulation to be effected by October 1st.</p>
                <p>General Youdenitch has recognized the independence of Esthonia on the condition
                    that the Esthonians will render all possible military aid to the Russian White
                    corps now operating to the east of Esthonia.</p>
                <p>The present program calls for an offensive against Petrograd by the Russians and
                    Esthonians and in which the Finns will cooperate by a simultaneous drive from
                    the Byeloostrov front.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Imbrie</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
